- There is no Google Tag Manager.

**My proposed line**

| Item | Verdict | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Per-application tracking links | **Build** | This is your actual goal. Use a `?ref=<company>` query param, which PostHog already records as a pageview property. It's about 10 lines, with no new service. |
| Dashboard | **Cut** | PostHog already has dashboards and insights. A filter on `ref` does the job. |
| Google Tag Manager | **Cut** | It duplicates PostHog and adds a second script, a consent burden and slower page loads. Nothing breaks without it. |
| A/B tests of the homepage | **Cut** | At 40 visits a week, a test needs months to detect anything but a huge effect. Recruiters also arrive with a link and a name, not as a random sample. |
